  "text": "**Alex:** Did you hear about the new caf\u00e9 opening on Main Street?\n\n**Jamie:** Yeah, I saw the sign. It says they serve vegan latte art. Is that even a thing?\n\n**Alex:** I think they pour the foam into shapes like leaves or hearts. It\u2019s pretty cool.\n\n**Jamie:** I\u2019d try it, but I\u2019m not sure I can handle the sugar rush. I\u2019m still recovering from last week\u2019s pastry binge.\n\n**Alex:** Ha, I know the feeling. I tried that cinnamon roll at the bakery and I was basically a human comma for a day.\n\n**Jamie:** Seriously? I thought I was being careful. The bread was so flaky, I didn\u2019t even notice until I was already halfway through.\n\n**Alex:** Yeah, and then you had to explain to your roommate why your couch had flour on it.\n\n**Jamie:** Oh, that was *not* my fault. That\u2019s what you get for letting me cook.\n\n**Alex:** Fair. But hey, maybe we should check out the caf\u00e9 this weekend? I\u2019ve been meaning to try something new.\n\n**Jamie:** Yeah, I\u2019m up for that. Just don\u2019t make me regret it like last time.\n\n**Alex:** No regrets, just good memories. Unless you count the time I accidentally burned the waffle.\n\n**Jamie:** That was *one* time. And it was *your* waffle, not mine.\n\n**Alex:** Okay, fair enough. Let\u2019s go. I\u2019ll buy the vegan latte. You can have the regular one.\n\n**Jamie:** Deal. But if I\u2019m not allowed to add extra syrup, I\u2019m not doing it.\n\n**Alex:** Not even a drop.",
